        <!-- 7. METHODOLOGY - collapsible -->
        <div class="calc-methodology">
          <button class="meth-toggle" onclick="toggleMethodology()" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Methodology &amp; sources</span>
            <span class="meth-arrow">&#9660;</span>
          </button>
          <div class="meth-body" id="meth-body" style="display:none">

            <p class="meth-section-head">Readiness cost model</p>
            <table class="meth-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>Value</th><th>Source / basis</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Annual tax compliance burden per company</td><td>~900h/year (384h research + 510h returns)</td><td><a href="https://www.vertexinc.com/resources/resource-library/gartner-global-e-invoicing-strategy-report" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Forrester TEI of Avalara (2024)</a> - per-company baseline for mid-sized EU firm</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Single-country e-invoicing go-live project duration</td><td>6–12 months</td><td>Billentis "Riding the Tornado" 2026 (Bruno Koch) - implementation timeline benchmark</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Readiness effort per mandate (internal prep only, excl. ERP config)</td><td>270–430h per mandate per entity</td><td>Derived from Avalara/Billentis anchors above; consistent with implementation partner project benchmarks. Not a single published benchmark - treated as internal estimate.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Structured team (low end)</td><td>270–290h</td><td>Organised ownership, clear mandate lead, proactive partner coordination</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Reactive team (high end)</td><td>405–430h</td><td>Distributed ownership, coordination overhead, post-go-live exception management</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <p class="meth-section-head">ERP multipliers</p>
            <table class="meth-table">
              <thead><tr><th>ERP</th><th>Multiplier</th><th>Entity scaling (2nd entity+)</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>NetSuite / Dynamics 365 / Other</td><td>×1.0</td><td>+15% per entity - multi-tenant cloud ERPs share PA provider setup, format mapping, and test scripts across entities; incremental work is entity registration, master data, and local training only</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Sage X3</td><td>×1.2 (estimated)</td><td>+25% per entity - directional estimate based on single-tenant architecture; no published benchmark. Higher UAT overhead for localised compliance patches vs. multi-tenant cloud ERPs</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Oracle Cloud ERP</td><td>×1.3 (estimated)</td><td>+40% per entity - directional estimate. Forrester ERP Solutions Landscape Q1 2026 cites higher configuration complexity for Oracle Fusion vs. lightweight cloud ERPs in regulatory compliance scenarios</td></tr>
                <tr><td>SAP S/4HANA</td><td>×1.5</td><td>+60% per entity - supported by SAPinsider S/4HANA Migration Benchmark 2025 and Forrester ERP Solutions Landscape Q1 2026 (higher "configuration complexity" rating)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Multi-ERP (2+ systems)</td><td>Avg multiplier ×1.135</td><td>+13.5% integration penalty - IDC 2025 "SaaS ERP Multi-Cloud Complexity" survey (12–15% integration and reconciliation penalty for heterogeneous ERP environments)</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

            <p class="meth-section-head">Hourly rates</p>
            <table class="meth-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Rate</th><th>Profile</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>€85/h</td><td>Lean finance team - <a href="https://www.roberthalf.com/be/en/insights/salary-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Robert Half 2026</a></td></tr>
                <tr><td>€100/h</td><td>Finance + Tax + ERP cross-functional - <a href="https://www.hays.com/salary-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hays 2026</a></td></tr>
                <tr><td>€120/h</td><td>Enterprise specialists - <a href="https://www.morganmckinley.com/salary-guides" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Morgan McKinley 2026</a></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <p style="margin-top:4px">Rates are fully loaded (1,650 productive hours/year). ERP reconfiguration and technical testing excluded.</p>

            <p class="meth-section-head">Country coverage — readiness hours (29 countries)</p>
            <p style="margin-top:0">Hours represent internal team time for readiness only: mandate research, ERP impact assessment, process design, and validation preparation. ERP reconfiguration, testing, and go-live support are excluded. Estimates are directional benchmarks for mid-market to enterprise companies, not project budgets. Source: Gemini Deep Research, May 2026, cross-referenced against Ardent Partners / Gartner 2024-26 ERP implementation benchmarks and OpenPeppol deployment data. Four complexity tiers: (1) CTC/clearance mandates with national APIs — France, Poland, Italy, Greece, Hungary, Croatia, Romania, Spain: 160–430h per entity. (2) Enhanced B2G with signature/certificate requirements — Portugal, Denmark, Slovakia: 150–900h. (3) Peppol standard B2G — Belgium, Netherlands, Sweden, Finland, Norway, Austria, Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania, Slovenia, Luxembourg, Switzerland: 80–500h. (4) ViDA horizon only — Czech Republic, Ireland, Bulgaria, Malta, Cyprus: 30–200h (impact assessment only).</p>

            <p class="meth-section-head">Annual compliance maintenance model</p>
            <p style="margin-top:0">Ongoing cost covers schema gap analysis and UAT for spec updates, API and certificate maintenance, regulatory change monitoring, and periodic compliance validation. Source: Gemini Deep Research, May 2026. Update frequency drives the range: CTC mandates (Poland KSeF, Greece myDATA, Italy SdI, Hungary RTIR, Croatia) update 1–2x/year with moderate-to-high internal response effort; Peppol mandates follow a bi-annual BIS 3.0 release cycle (May/November) with lower effort. Monitoring hours are scaled by entity count but not by ERP multiplier — ongoing maintenance is primarily operational, not configuration work.</p>

            <p class="meth-section-head">Annual mandate burden</p>
            <p>Mandate readiness is recurring, not one-time. <a href="https://www.vertexinc.com/resources/resource-library/navigating-urgent-e-invoicing-mandates-december-2025-regulatory-alert" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vertex Regulatory Tracker (Jan 2026)</a> recorded 11 significant regulatory events across France, Poland, Belgium, Spain, Latvia, and Greece in Q4 2025 alone: new technical schemas, pilot launches, legal amendments, and enforcement date confirmations. For a 4–6 country EU footprint, this suggests 4–7+ significant events per year is a conservative floor, not a ceiling. Event types carry different effort weights: go-live events (~100% readiness effort), schema/format updates (~40%), legislative tuning (~20%). Annual estimate uses 2.5–3.5 full-mandate equivalents per year. Note: the Sovos and Billentis reports are cited as general sources for EU mandate complexity; neither report contains the specific per-company frequency figure.</p>

            <p class="meth-section-head">Penalty exposure</p>
            <table class="meth-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Penalty</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>France</td><td>€50/invoice, capped €15,000/year/entity</td><td>France 2026 Budget Law (approved Feb 2026) - <a href="https://www.dynatos.com/blog/france-e-invoicing-penalties-enforcement-2026/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dynatos 2026</a>; <a href="https://sovos.com/regulatory-updates/vat/france-approves-2026-budget-law-confirming-key-amendments-to-the-e-invoicing-and-e-reporting-mandate/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sovos France Budget Law</a></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Poland (KSeF)</td><td>100% of VAT per invoice, no cap (post Jan 2027)</td><td><a href="https://ksef.podatki.gov.pl/informacje-ogolne-ksef-20/podstawy-prawne-oraz-kluczowe-terminy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Art. 106ni VAT Act</a></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Germany</td><td>Up to €5,000/invoice (§26a UStG); GoBD non-compliance: VAT deduction denial, bookkeeping rejection; no fixed fine, tax authority discretion (AO)</td><td><a href="https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/ustg_1980/__26a.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">§26a UStG (official text)</a>; <a href="https://www.bundesfinanzministerium.de/Content/DE/FAQ/e-rechnung.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BMF E-Rechnung FAQ</a></td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>

          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


